  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Crlp/4653/2022 on 15 July, 2022 The Hon'Ble Sri Justice Subba Reddy Satti Criminal Petition No.4653 of 2022 Order:",
    "facts": "Accused No.2 in Crime No.100 of 2022 of Pullala Cheruvu Police Station, Prakasham District, filed the above criminal petition under Section 438 of Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (for short \"Cr.P.C.,\") seeking pre-arrest bail. 2. The case of the prosecution is that on 29.05.2022, raid party while conducting search found the place where ID liquor is being manufactured. Since nobody was found at the scene of offence, no mediators report was prepared. Basing on the report lodged by Head Constable, the present crime is registered for the offence punishable under Section 7(A) read with 8(E) of the Andhra Pradesh Prohibition (Amendment) Act, 2020.",
    "arguments": "3. Heard Sri Eluru Sesha Mahesh Babu, learned counsel for the petitioner and learned Special Assistant Public Prosecutor for State. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that petitioner is Proprietor of Seetha Ramaiah Kirana Shop and he placed a copy of license with reference No.30220529110700932, dated 29.05.2022 issued by Government of Andhra Pradesh, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, Food Safety Compliance System is placed before this Court. Learned counsel submits that petitioner obtained requisite license and certificates from the concerned departments for doing kirana business and petitioner is no way concerned with the alleged offence and he is falsely implicated in the crime only basing on the confession of co-accused. Learned counsel places reliance on G.O.Ms.No.149 dated 18.04.2017 issued by Revenue (Excise- II) Department and submits that as per the guidelines framed therein, jaggery or black jaggery is not a prohibited commodity and mere possession, selling or transportation shall not amount to commission an offence. He would contend that the petitioner is not aware for which purpose jaggery was purchased from him. Hence, he prays to grant pre-arrest bail to the petitioner. 5. Learned Special Assistant Public Prosecutor submits opposed the bail application on the ground that investigation is pending.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Heard Sri Eluru Sesha Mahesh Babu, learned counsel for the petitioner and learned Special Assistant Public Prosecutor for State. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that petitioner is Proprietor of Seetha Ramaiah Kirana Shop and he placed a copy of license with reference No.30220529110700932, dated 29.05.2022 issued by Government of Andhra Pradesh, Food Safety and Standards Authority of India, Food Safety Compliance System is placed before this Court. Learned counsel submits that petitioner obtained requisite license and certificates from the concerned departments for doing kirana business and petitioner is no way concerned with the alleged offence and he is falsely implicated in the crime only basing on the confession of co-accused. Learned counsel places reliance on G.O.Ms.No.149 dated 18.04.2017 issued by Revenue (Excise- II) Department and submits that as per the guidelines framed therein, jaggery or black jaggery is not a prohibited commodity and mere possession, selling or transportation shall not amount to commission an offence. He would contend that the petitioner is not aware for which purpose jaggery was purchased from him.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Hence, he prays to grant pre-arrest bail to the petitioner. 5. Learned Special Assistant Public Prosecutor submits opposed the bail application on the ground that investigation is pending.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
